INT. ICE-FISHING HUT - NIGHT

Tin walls ticking with frost. A propane lantern. A square hole in the floor shows black water. A radio on a shelf hisses.

BRENNA TALLCHIEF, thirties, huddles in a parka, a thermos shaking in both hands. She has not slept. The ice groans somewhere under the hut and she flinches.

The radio crackles.

RANGER (V.O.)
(over radio)
Hut Four, Hut Four, this is Ranger Station. Do you copy?

Brenna lunges for the handset.

BRENNA
Copy! Copy, I'm here!

RANGER (V.O.)
Ice is breaking up on the east side. You need to move.

BRENNA
He's out on it! My brother's out on it!

RANGER (V.O.)
Say again?

The door bangs open. A blast of snow. SOL TALLCHIEF, twenty, bursts in, soaked to the thighs, lugging a sled.

BRENNA (CONT'D)
Sol!

She hauls him in by the collar. He drops the sled. Falls to his knees. The ice booms under them, one long cracking roar.

SOL
Go. Go!

She seizes the radio. He grabs the lantern. The floor tilts.

BRENNA
(into handset)
We're leaving. We're leaving now.

RANGER (V.O.)
Copy. Godspeed.

They burst out through the door.
